        "date": "2026-11-21T10:21:11Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): declare OpType::VCarve at the enum's end, where its row is\n\nThe held work declared VCarve after Engrave, but its table row and tag\nare appended at 44. OpType as usize is the table row everywhere, so each\nlater kind read the row of its neighbour (a ribbon cell made the wrong\nkind). The registry pin caught it; the declaration now follows the row.\n\nThe kind-table pins take the new kind: the registry count is 45, the\nlathe voice refuses 32 kinds, the tilt slot covers VCarve, a reduced\nmodel refuses it as it refuses Engrave, and the ribbon names VCarve as\nthe tail.\n\nRefs #1443\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
